  abstract  = { Abstract In many contexts such as validation of XML data, software model checking and parametrized verification, the systems studied are naturally abstracted as finite state automata, but whose input alphabet is infinite. The use of such automata for verification requires their non-emptiness problems to be decidable. However, ensuring this is non-trivial, since the space of configurations of such automata is infinite. We describe some recent attempts in this direction, and suggest that an entire theoretical framework awaits development. }
